     "body": {
      "content": [
       {
        "content": [
         {
          "text": "The problem appears to be right here:  ",
          "type": "text"
         },
         {
          "marks": [
           {
            "attrs": {
             "href": "https://github.com/fcrepo4/fcrepo4/blob/master/fcrepo-kernel-modeshape/src/main/java/org/fcrepo/kernel/modeshape/NonRdfSourceDescriptionImpl.java#L80"
            },
            "type": "link"
           }
          ],
          "text": "https://github.com/fcrepo4/fcrepo4/blob/master/fcrepo-kernel-modeshape/src/main/java/org/fcrepo/kernel/modeshape/NonRdfSourceDescriptionImpl.java#L80",
          "type": "text"
         },
         {
          "text": ".  In order to resolve the list of description mementos, it appears that each memento description is being loaded and the getContent() method is being called on each one of those description mementos.   The current code attempts to resolve that content node by getting the binary memento with a matching timestamp.  If no such memento exists,  as is the case when a binary description memento is created independent from the binary itself,  a PathNotFoundException is thrown.",
          "type": "text"
         }
        ],
        "type": "paragraph"
       }
      ],
      "type": "doc",
      "version": 1
     },
